WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.969
-Could we just run down
everything that's

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.937
happened to you since
you were last on our show?

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:06.106
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.140
-You won an Oscar for
"12 Years a Slave."

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.174
-Not bad.
-Yeah, not bad.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.275
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.544
You were in a couple of
small films --

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:14.981
"Star Wars" and "Black Panther."

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.282
You got a Tony nomination...
-Mm-hmm!

00:00:17.282 --> 00:00:18.317
-...for your -- Yeah.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:19.919
And then probably
most important --

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.654
your name is now
a Beyoncé lyric.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.756
-I mean, yeah.
-I mean, come on. That's --

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:26.125
-Yeah, that's it.
-How fun is that?

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:28.127
"Brown Skin Girl" -- she says,

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.229
"She needs an Oscar
for that pretty dark skin.

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:32.398
Pretty like Lupita when the
cameras close in."

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.634
Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.636
I love that!

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.037
Now, how do you hear about that?

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.506
Does Beyoncé call you and give
you a heads-up that she --

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:44.510
-No! Queen Bee does not tell
anyone anything.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:49.149
No, I was in London
and I was doing a press junket

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:52.918
for a documentary I did called
"Warrior Women."

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:56.489
And the first journalist
is just interviewing me,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.556
and she says, "How do you feel

00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:59.225
now that you're
a Beyoncé lyric?"

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.626
And I was like,
"What are you talking about?"

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:03.530
And she was like, "Really?
It dropped this morning.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.563
You don't know?"

00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:06.198
And I was like,
"No, I don't know.

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:07.867
What are you talking about?"
"Oh, my God!

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.168
Am I the first person
to tell you?"

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:10.169
And I was like, "Yes, you are."

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.138
-"You're an absolute
lyric right now.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.474
Yeah, it's madness."
-She was so chuffed.

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.277
-Yeah. But you're also --

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.845
I found out,
you're a Jay-Z lyric, as well.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.482
-I am, yes!
-What's going on with the...

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:26.252
[ Cheers and applause ]
They're obsessed.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.253
What's going on with
the Carters?

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.421
-I don't know.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.623
I love the Carters,
and they seem to love me.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.958
I'm not mad.
-Do you like anyone better?

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:36.228
Which song do you like --
-Oh, no, I couldn't do that.

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:38.598
I couldn't choose
between the two, no.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.199
-I've heard you rap before.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.635
You rap,
but what do you rap under?

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.537
A different name, right?
-Yes.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.139
-Well, who are you?
-Troublemaker.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:48.507
-Ah! That's what
I'm talking about.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:51.010
Yeah, Troublemaker.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:55.047
Could you give us
a little sample of a rap?

00:01:55.047 --> 00:02:00.053
-I mean...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.421
-Come on.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.188
-Well, the thing -- Okay,
the thing about Troublemaker --

00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:05.825
first of all, I was baptized
Troublemaker by Common,

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.160
so I feel like it's legit.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.661
-Wow.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.397
-And it's something I do
in a car.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.531
I need a car.

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:15.702
But, okay, if I had a mic,
like, a mic --

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:18.070
Oh, and every respectable -- Oh!

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.806
-We always have --
We have so many microphones.

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:22.909
Whichever one you want to use.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.877
-Yeah, a respectable emcee
has that.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:27.680
But then, also, one of
the things I have to have

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.084
as Troublemaker is shades, so --
Oh, my God.

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:36.189
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.658
-Just give -- Just a taste.
Just a taste.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.759
-Oh, my goodness.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.995
Okay, only if The Roots
will join me!

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:48.368
♪♪
Oh, boy. Oh, boy. Oh!

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:53.472
That's a dope beat. Okay.
Hold up.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:56.309
♪ Troublemaker
in the building, hey ♪

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.210
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.913
♪ I feel some bars coming ♪
♪ Bars coming ♪

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:02.514
♪ Oh-oh ♪

00:03:02.514 --> 00:03:05.518
♪ Much love to the Carters,
Hova and Beyoncé ♪

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.353
♪ They always big me up
in a big way ♪

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.522
♪ I'm a brown-skin girl,
so that means a lot ♪

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.591
♪ Hov said we made it,
got an Oscar for my props ♪

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.860
♪ Much love to Jimmy and
The Roots 'cause they hot ♪

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.995
♪ Wrote a book about self-love,
"Sulwe" is 'bout to drop ♪

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:18.464
♪ October 15th, on time,
tick-tock ♪

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.666
♪ Better go to commercial or
these bars won't stop ♪

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:24.169
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, yes! Wow!

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:27.906
Hey! You can do it. Yeah!

00:03:27.906 --> 00:03:33.512
That was amazing! Troublemaker!
Oh, I love it!

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:36.048
Dude, come on.
Song of the summer.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.617
Let's see more Troublemaker.
I love it, pal.

00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:40.352
Thank you for doing that.
-I'm a one-hit wonder.

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:42.655
-No, I loved that.
-Thank you.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.790
-Did you used to do that --

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.925
Like, do you do
that on set and, like --

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:48.327
I mean, do you perform
all the time?

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:51.598
-I'm a fraud.
-You are a fraud.

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:54.400
-I mean, I feel like
in my past li--

00:03:54.400 --> 00:04:01.874
I am supposed to be a rapper,
but I'm not.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:05.344
-You're not.
-So I just -- I do it for fun.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:09.816
I like to play a rapper, but
I'm really not one.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.551
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
I thought that was fantastic.

